{"timestamp":"2026-08-08T16:01:00.073Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Created the Rust port in `/output` as a std-only 2021 Cargo package. The entry file is [test11.rs](/output/test11.rs), and the implementation is organized under [inflection/mod.rs](/output/inflection/mod.rs:1) and [inflection/inflector.rs](/output/inflection/inflector.rs:1). It matches the C++ program’s observed behavior, including `atoi`-style argument parsing and byte-based truncation for non-ASCII input.\n\nI compiled it both ways:\n`cargo build --release` -> [target/release/test11](/output/target/release/test11)\n`rustc --edition=2021 test11.rs -o test11` -> [test11](/output/test11)\n\nI also byte-compared both Rust binaries against `/workspace/dataset/test11_executable` on representative cases including empty strings, separators, Unicode truncation, and integer overflow inputs. All matched.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
